One vectorized mini-batch update (w includes bias w0 separately):
Given Xb shape (B,d), yb shape (B,), w shape (d,), b scalar:
pred = Xb @ w + b; errors = (yb - pred);
w += eta * (Xb.T @ errors); b += eta * errors.sum();
Optionally scale by B (use mean) depending on your cost definition.
This generalizes the vectorized AdalineGD update (X.T.dot(errors)) to batches and matches the per-sample AdalineSGD idea while staying vectorized. Source for batch-style update pattern: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rasbt/python-machine-learning-book-3rd-edition/master/ch02/ch02.py
